
  Usage on your Ubuntu box:

  # One-time setup
  sudo apt install ansible python3-libvirt python3-lxml
  ansible-galaxy collection install community.libvirt

  # Run
  cd docs/freebsd-port/ansible
  ansible-playbook playbooks/01-setup-host.yml --ask-become-pass
  ansible-playbook playbooks/02-configure-freebsd.yml
  ansible-playbook playbooks/03-deploy-tigerbeetle.yml
  ansible-playbook playbooks/04-cluster-ops.yml -e operation=start

  Key wins over bash:
  - Idempotent: Re-run safely, skips already-done work
  - SSH native: No more ssh root@... "command" loops
  - --check flag: Dry run to see what would change
  - Config separated: group_vars/all.yml instead of hardcoded variables scattered through script
  - Parallelism built-in: Can run on all nodes simultaneously
